[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   step_165: canonical disformal transport benchmark and geometry controls.
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   Fits the step-065 unsigned equivalent-time amplitude using the positive-B
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   benchmark envelope b(u)=B0*u^2/(1+u^2)*exp(-u^4/(2*sigma_B^4)). The leading
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   connection term is integrated in a radial boundary layer. This is a scale
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   requirement, not a derived admissible normalization or field solution.
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   Per-comet radial speeds are computed from the residual cohort's inverse
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   semimajor axes and angular momenta at 250 AU. Spatial entry and exit directions
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   come from the published original/future conic planes. Near-parabolic orbits
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   cross near the same aphelion-side region; they are not antipodal. The previous
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   antipodal construction imposed generic odd-mode cancellation artificially.
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   The exploratory signed-dipole excursion G(theta)=cos(theta) has an even
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   quartic amplitude in the coincident-aphelion limit because the envelope is
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   even and the traversal gradient is squared. Offset dipoles and quadrupolar
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   profiles are retained as comparison cases. Shape correlations are conditional
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   on this model exploration, not calibrated discovery probabilities.
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   The signed transport and unsigned fitted statistic are stored separately.
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   Clock and one-crossing impulse comparisons are conditional diagnostics; the
[2026-10-17 16:46:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 165]   full metric, trajectory and observation response remains to be validated.
